\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.png}{options: style='float: right' alt='' width='120'}}

CorNetto provides a Bioconductor-oriented workflow for constructing
knowledge-guided correlation networks from normalized multi-omic
abundance data. The package is designed around
\code{MultiAssayExperiment::MultiAssayExperiment()} so that multiple assays
and their shared sample metadata can be analysed consistently.

The main workflow includes:
\itemize{
\item validation of normalized assay inputs
\item pre-analysis summaries of missingness, sample counts, and feature counts
\item sample and feature filtering before network construction
\item group-specific correlation networks
\item differential correlation, over all pairs in an assay or over
prior-supported candidate edges
\item rewiring score calculation
\item permutation-based assessment of rewiring scores
\item pathway-focused network extraction
\item graph creation and Cytoscape-ready export
}

The vignette (\code{vignette("CorNetto")}) opens with a diagram of how these
fit together.
}
